  "text": "For a material transition, each admission owner derives and validates the complete enclosing relation from authoritative inputs, including every materially deciding participant, equality join and far-side seam. Caller assertions of completeness, authority or prior admission are insufficient. Bind one exact current authoritative basis through semantic commit, or an explicitly coherent composite basis; if currentness can advance, condition commit on predecessor/currentness or re-enter without effect. Validate every participant before any effect. Direct and supported composite/nested paths admit the whole transition or none, never a subset or competing same-scope path. Standing proof covers supported forged/ambiguous/stale/mixed-basis/rival-authority cases, fresh reconstruction and exact replay, plus failure at each materially distinct publication boundary (or a declared covering equivalence/dominance proof). Final validation failure is not post-validation atomic-failure evidence. Unsupported cases need design-grounded exclusion, not a helper's inability to construct them.",
