        ],
        "statement": "Causal triage distinguishes defective realization under adequate unchanged law, inadequate requirement/design, inaccurate predictive model and insufficient observation. Use evidence that distinguishes causes over the same exact subject and basis. Their lawful routes remain different. A failed candidate alone does not establish inadequate governing law. For insufficient observation, acquire the missing admissible observation through its authorized route, or retain indeterminate and withhold the dependent claim. Repetition of the same uninformative check supplies no missing evidence.",
